  "question": {
    "text": "The degree of dissociation $(\\alpha)$ of a weak electrolyte, $A_x B_y$ is related to van't Hoff factor (i) by the expression:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\alpha=\\frac{i-1}{x+y+1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\alpha=\\frac{x+y-1}{i-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\alpha=\\frac{x+y+1}{i-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\alpha=\\frac{i-1}{(x+y-1)}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& i=1-\\alpha+n \\alpha=1+\\alpha(n-1) \\\\\n& \\frac{i-1}{n-1}=\\alpha \\\\\n& A_x B_y \\rightarrow x A^{+y}+y B^{-x} \\\\\n& n=x+y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSo $\\alpha=\\frac{i-1}{x+y-1}$"
  }
}